# L §3.1 (a record literal names its type's fields), §8.3 LOAD-FIELD `field <f> twice` (tally 2.1.6, issue #64): a
# record row naming x twice is refused, so no reader can take one x and another reader the other. A pinning test:
# tally 2.1.5's refcore refused it so already, without the form in the catalogue.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input r: (x int, y int)

ask q: r.x

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r = (x: 1, x: 2, y: 3)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-FIELD field x twice (m.tally:17)
